  "body": "### Summary\n\nCamCraft's UI gets its workbench rework, built on upstream v0.19.0. It gives the shell a light workbench theme (`horizon-day`), puts a tab row above the ribbon cells to switch machine modes in one click, gives the operation page's section tabs their own glyphs, tightens the browser's chrome and row order, and adds camera tools to the viewport's floating control ribbon.\n\nRefs #1677 (the workbench rework track; follow-up #1678 removes the unreachable Machine-door code).\n\nChangelog: UI — changed the density of the built-in themes' shipped tokens: `cell_h` 40 -> 30, `cell_w` 72 -> 76, `glyph_px` 24 -> 16, `font_label` 13 -> 11, kept so the ribbon's caption row still fits the tab strip; the ribbon height stays 66 px (`RIBBON_TAB_H + cell_h + 20.0`). Pointer tests re-anchored to the compacted browser header. Horizon Day opts into the same density and the light palette.\n\nFive commits, one topic each:\n\n- `feat(ui): a light workbench theme and workspace tabs`\n- `feat(ui): the operation page's section tabs wear their own glyphs`\n- `feat(ui): a compact browser header and ordered rows`\n- `feat(ui): camera tools in the viewport's control ribbon`\n- `refactor(ui): drop the Machine ribbon cell - the workspace tabs own the switch`\n\n### Before (upstream f2b42e3d) / after (this branch)\n\nBoth windows show a fresh document at the same 100% size with the default dark theme and the default document: the 1280-point floor, 250% display scale.\n\n![before: upstream v0.19.0](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ahmetv10/Camcraft/feat/camcraft-ui/docs/images/pr-1639-workbench/before.png)\n\n![after: this branch](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ahmetv10/Camcraft/feat/camcraft-ui/docs/images/pr-1639-workbench/after.png)\n\n### Density change to the built-in themes\n\nBefore this PR, the built-in dark and light columns shipped `cell_h` 40.0, `cell_w` 72.0, `glyph_px` 24.0 and `font_label` 13.0. They now ship 30.0 / 76.0 / 16.0 / 11.0, matching the Horizon Day accent's intended density. The ribbon height is unchanged at 66 px. The change is kept deliberately (a tighter default that still reads at 11 px), and is called out here rather than hidden in the token table.\n\n### What to look at\n\n- The ribbon gains a workspace tab row above the cells: one tab per machine mode in `machine_modes::MACHINE_MODES`, switching through the same undoable `LoadBuiltinMachine` the Machine door queued. The stocked door and the tabs were two doors onto one switch; the tabs won, and the SETUP group sheds the redundant \"Machine\" cell at the end. The Machine door's code path remains present but unreachable from the UI, tracked in #1678 for removal.\n- `assets/themes/horizon-day.json` is a light \"Horizon Day\" palette (base light). Nothing switches the default theme; dark remains the default.\n- The section tabs in the operation pages wear purpose-drawn `sec-*` glyphs (six SVG masters, rendered at the ribbon's token size; our own artwork); the ribbon cell ink gains a tinted-palette hook with a steel-blue tint for command glyphs.\n- The viewport's floating control ribbon gains four buttons: a Perspective/Orthographic toggle (the View door's radios' true twin), and a latched Orbit/Pan/Zoom nav tool that owns the drag whatever the mouse button — a latched tool's click is no click at all.\n- The browser heads with one chrome row (a View door, Expand all / Collapse all) and the setup's furniture leads the rows: Setups, WCS, Stock, Operations, Tool list, Fixtures, Machine, Post.\n\n### Verification\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` — 772 passed. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` — green (ui suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --lib --tests` — no warnings.\n\nKnown flake: the palette/assertion law tests are parallel-order dependent; a full parallel run can see a handful of them fail while `--test-threads=1` is all green. Serial runs pass. Nothing in this PR changes their behaviour; re-run to confirm.\n\nGate logs: `gate-logs/quick-20261114-*` (not committed).\n",
